::JOUR_U01_L04_Q01::[MLA.JOUR.MED.08] Which design choice best supports audience understanding? {
=A. A headline that clearly names the verified update#Correct. This answer applies the lesson standard to journalism practice.
~B. An unrelated image placed first#Review the scenario and standard. This choice does not best support accurate journalism practice.
~C. Tiny text for the main fact#Review the scenario and standard. This choice does not best support accurate journalism practice.
~D. A caption with no names or context#Review the scenario and standard. This choice does not best support accurate journalism practice.
}
::JOUR_U01_L04_Q02::[MLA.JOUR.DIG.03] Visual accuracy means images should: {
~A. create a false impression if dramatic#Review the scenario and standard. This choice does not best support accurate journalism practice.
=B. truthfully represent the subject and context#Correct. This answer applies the lesson standard to journalism practice.
~C. avoid captions always#Review the scenario and standard. This choice does not best support accurate journalism practice.
~D. replace source checking#Review the scenario and standard. This choice does not best support accurate journalism practice.
}
::JOUR_U01_L04_Q03::[MLA.JOUR.ETH.01] A format-specific digital news post should: {
~A. use only decoration#Review the scenario and standard. This choice does not best support accurate journalism practice.
~B. hide the source#Review the scenario and standard. This choice does not best support accurate journalism practice.
=C. match the platform while keeping information accurate#Correct. This answer applies the lesson standard to journalism practice.
~D. ignore audience needs#Review the scenario and standard. This choice does not best support accurate journalism practice.
}
::JOUR_U01_L04_Q04::[MLA.JOUR.MED.08] A layout uses design hierarchy when it: {
~A. places all details randomly#Review the scenario and standard. This choice does not best support accurate journalism practice.
~B. makes decoration more important than facts#Review the scenario and standard. This choice does not best support accurate journalism practice.
~C. removes the headline#Review the scenario and standard. This choice does not best support accurate journalism practice.
=D. guides readers to the most important information first#Correct. This answer applies the lesson standard to journalism practice.
}
::JOUR_U01_L04_Q05::[MLA.JOUR.DIG.03] A misleading photo choice is one that: {
=A. suggests a problem or event not supported by the article#Correct. This answer applies the lesson standard to journalism practice.
~B. shows the actual event accurately#Review the scenario and standard. This choice does not best support accurate journalism practice.
~C. has a factual caption#Review the scenario and standard. This choice does not best support accurate journalism practice.
~D. matches the verified story#Review the scenario and standard. This choice does not best support accurate journalism practice.
}
::JOUR_U01_L04_Q06::[MLA.JOUR.MED.08] Why should a caption identify who, what, when, or where? {
~A. Captions should be mysterious.#Review the scenario and standard. This choice does not best support accurate journalism practice.
~B. Captions replace the whole article.#Review the scenario and standard. This choice does not best support accurate journalism practice.
=C. Captions are part of factual journalism, not decoration.#Correct. This answer applies the lesson standard to journalism practice.
~D. Captions should exaggerate.#Review the scenario and standard. This choice does not best support accurate journalism practice.
}
::JOUR_U01_L04_Q07::[MLA.JOUR.MED.08] Which platform-fit choice works best for a quick social update? {
~A. Three dense paragraphs in tiny text#Review the scenario and standard. This choice does not best support accurate journalism practice.
=B. Clear headline, short verified facts, and link to details#Correct. This answer applies the lesson standard to journalism practice.
~C. A random stock image only#Review the scenario and standard. This choice does not best support accurate journalism practice.
~D. No source or date#Review the scenario and standard. This choice does not best support accurate journalism practice.
}
::JOUR_U01_L04_Q08::[MLA.JOUR.ETH.01] Which design decision protects format-specific quality? {
~A. Choosing the brightest image regardless of accuracy#Review the scenario and standard. This choice does not best support accurate journalism practice.
~B. Cropping out important context#Review the scenario and standard. This choice does not best support accurate journalism practice.
~C. Using a caption from another event#Review the scenario and standard. This choice does not best support accurate journalism practice.
=D. Using visuals that fit the story purpose and verified facts#Correct. This answer applies the lesson standard to journalism practice.
}
::JOUR_U01_L04_Q09::[MLA.JOUR.MED.08] Visual culture trends affect journalism because audiences often expect: {
=A. clear images, scannable layout, and digital access#Correct. This answer applies the lesson standard to journalism practice.
~B. no facts in digital media#Review the scenario and standard. This choice does not best support accurate journalism practice.
~C. unlabeled visuals only#Review the scenario and standard. This choice does not best support accurate journalism practice.
~D. fictional graphics#Review the scenario and standard. This choice does not best support accurate journalism practice.
}
